You can now route agent requests to self-hosted open-weight models using a[custom model gateway](https://mastra.ai/models/gateways/custom-gateways) . Give the gateway a custom ID, then use it as the` model` prefix in your agent's config:` private/ollama/gpt-oss:20b` .


Your browser does not support the video tag.A research agent in Studio runs on gpt-oss:20b through the gateway while the ollama serve logs show each request arrive locally, then the agent answers with a guide to deploying the model on AWS.


Using a hosted provider service can complicate HIPAA or GDPR compliance (unless data retention agreements are in place). Self-hosting removes the third party, preventing sensitive data from reaching models outside of your network.


Costs may also be reduced as you're only paying for infrastructure, not tokens, and you control which models your agents can use.


To hide external providers from Studio's model picker, set` AUTO_BLOCK_EXTERNAL_PROVIDERS=true` in your` .env` so users can only select models from your own gateways.


## Get started


Install the latest` @mastra/core` and an AI SDK provider for your gateway's API:


Terminal


```text
npm   install   @mastra/core@latest   @ai-sdk/openai-compatible@3.0.84
```


note


Requires` @mastra/core@1.82.0` or later, added in[PR #18153](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/pull/18153) .


## Run a local model


This example uses Ollama and[gpt-oss:20b](https://ollama.com/library/gpt-oss:20b) . Running` ollama serve` starts the server, with an OpenAI-compatible API at` http://localhost:11434/v1` :


Terminal


```text
brew   install   ollama
ollama   pull   gpt-oss:20b
ollama   serve
```


## Create a gateway


Create a gateway that sends every model call to the local Ollama server:


- ` id` : The model ID prefix, e.g.` private` in` private/ollama/gpt-oss:20b` .
- ` name` : The gateway's display name.
- ` fetchProviders()` : Returns the providers and models the gateway offers, listed in Studio's model picker.
- ` buildUrl()` : Returns the base URL for model calls.
- ` getApiKey()` : Returns the API key to send with each call (not required for local models).
- ` resolveLanguageModel()` : Creates the language model for each call.


src/mastra/gateways/private-gateway.ts


```text
import   {   createOpenAICompatible   }   from   "  @ai-sdk/openai-compatible  "  ;
import   type   {   MastraModelGatewayInterface   }   from   "  @mastra/core/llm  "  ;


export   const   privateGateway  :   MastraModelGatewayInterface   =   {
id:   "  private  "  ,
name:   "  Private Gateway  "  ,
fetchProviders  :   async   ()   =>   {
return   {
ollama: {
name:   "  Ollama  "  ,
models: [  "  gpt-oss:20b  "  ],
apiKeyEnvVar: [],
gateway:   "  private  "  ,
url:   "  http://localhost:11434/v1  "
}
};
},
buildUrl  : ()   =>   {
return   "  http://localhost:11434/v1  "  ;
},
getApiKey  :   async   ()   =>   {
return   ""  ;
},
resolveLanguageModel  : ({ modelId, providerId, apiKey })   =>   {
return   createOpenAICompatible  ({
name: providerId,
apiKey,
baseURL:   "  http://localhost:11434/v1  "
}).  chatModel  (modelId);
}
};
```


## Register the gateway


Add the gateway to your Mastra instance:


src/mastra/index.ts


```text
export   const   mastra   =   new   Mastra  ({
// ...
gateways: { privateGateway }
});
```


## Use the model


Reference the model by` \[gatewayId\]/\[provider\]/\[model\]` :


src/mastra/agents/research-agent.ts


```text
export   const   researchAgent   =   new   Agent  ({
id:   "  research-agent  "  ,
name:   "  Research Agent  "  ,
instructions:   /* ... */  ,
model:   "  private/ollama/gpt-oss:20b  "
});
```


## Hide external providers in Studio


Add the variable to your` .env` :


.env


```text
AUTO_BLOCK_EXTERNAL_PROVIDERS  =  true
```


For more information and full configuration options, see:


- [Custom model gateways](https://mastra.ai/models/gateways/custom-gateways)
- [When to use custom gateways](https://mastra.ai/models/gateways/custom-gateways#when-to-use-custom-gateways)
- [Showing only custom gateways in Studio](https://mastra.ai/models/gateways/custom-gateways#showing-only-custom-gateways-in-studio)
- [Gateway-owned authentication](https://mastra.ai/models/gateways/custom-gateways#gateway-owned-authentication)
- [Model pricing](https://mastra.ai/models/gateways/custom-gateways#model-pricing)
